2. Harmonized System nomenclature (inside hs.json)
--------------------------------------------------
The `desc` field of hs.json contains Harmonized System commodity descriptions.
The Harmonized System nomenclature is a work of the World Customs Organization
(WCO), which asserts copyright over it.

  https://www.wcoomd.org/

These descriptions are redistributed here as obtained from UN Comtrade's
public reference endpoint. Obtaining them from UN Comtrade does not by itself
convey WCO redistribution rights. If you fork, repackage, or ship this project
commercially, verify your position with the WCO first — or drop hs.json and
have refresh_reference.py fetch it at install time.


3. Derived Korean-language indexes (this project's own work)
------------------------------------------------------------
Files:
  references/hs_ko.json
  references/country_aliases_ko.json
  references/country_names_ko.json

These map Korean product and country names onto HS/M49 codes. The mapping is
original work by this project and is covered by LICENSE. The codes themselves
are the public identifiers described above.


4. Korea trading-partner snapshot
---------------------------------
File:
  references/kr-top-partners.json

Derived from UN Comtrade query results (reporter=KOR, cmdCode=TOTAL, flow=X).
It is an aggregate ranking, not a reproduction of the underlying dataset.

Regenerate:
  python3 .../scripts/refresh_reference.py partners


5. Test fixtures — NOT distributed
----------------------------------
tests/fixtures/cache/ holds raw UN Comtrade API responses (actual trade
values). Those are the publisher's data, not ours, so they are deliberately
excluded from version control via .gitignore.

Contributors generate them locally before running the suite:
  python3 tests/record_fixtures.py


